<BaseLayout lang="en" path="/en/" title="Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov (Antiokh) — IT Manager" description="Anton Nazarov: 18 years in IT, engineering management, systems architecture, and complex implementation. Biography, track record, and real project portfolio.">
  <section class="portrait-hero wrap"><div class="portrait-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Belgrade · working worldwide</div><p class="hello">My name is</p><h1>Anton<br />Nazarov.</h1><p class="hero-role">IT manager, systems architect, and the person people call when <em>“it’s complicated.”</em></p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button solid" href="#story">My story ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/en/projects/">View 21 projects →</a></div></div><figure class="portrait"><img src="/anton-nazarov.png" alt="Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov, IT manager and systems architect" /><figcaption><span>Antiokh</span><span>Photo to be updated</span></figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="manifesto dark-section"><div class="wrap"><p class="section-label">In one paragraph</p><blockquote>“I don’t sell AI as magic or draw architecture for the diagram. I need a system that survives the demo, the second employee, and its first serious failure.”</blockquote><div class="manifesto-notes"><p>I started as an enterprise developer. Then I learned that code is rarely the hardest part.</p><p>The harder work is agreeing on meaning, seeing the real process, carrying change through resistance, and staying with people after launch.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="story" class="story wrap"><div class="story-aside"><span class="section-label">The story / 2008—now</span><h2>I did not climb a single career ladder.</h2></div><div class="story-body"><p class="story-lead">Development taught me to build. Banking taught me to see processes. Government taught me alignment. ZIL taught me responsibility for people and continuity. Independent work brought it all into one outcome.</p><p>The same story kept repeating: enter a place where processes live in people’s heads, spreadsheets, and chats; find the breaks; turn implicit rules into a model; build the system; help it take root.</p></div></section>
  <section class="career"><div class="wrap"><div class="career-list">{timeline.map(([date,kicker,title,text],i)=><article class="career-item"><div class="career-date">{date}</div><div class="career-mark">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</div><div><span>{kicker}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div></article>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="numbers dark-section"><div class="wrap number-grid"><div><b>18</b><span>years of professional experience</span></div><div><b>145</b><span>employees in ZIL’s IT environment</span></div><div><b>100+</b><span>institutions in one system</span></div><div><b>×13</b><span>client revenue growth after automation</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="real-work"><div class="wrap"><div class="portfolio-intro"><span class="section-label">Not a screen gallery / real cases</span><h2>What I actually<br />did.</h2><p>Context, personal responsibility, decisions, and outcomes — no anonymous “we developed.”</p></div>{cases.map((item,i)=><article class:list={['feature-case',i%2&&'reverse']} id={item.id}><div class="feature-visual"><img src={item.image} alt={`${item.title} interface`} loading="lazy" /><span>{item.number}</span></div><div class="feature-copy"><p class="case-tag">{item.tag}</p><h3>{item.title}</h3><p class="case-lead">{item.lead}</p><p>{item.text}</p><div class="case-proof">My role: {item.proof}</div><a href={`/en/projects/#${item.id}`}>Read the case →</a></div></article>)}<div class="all-work"><p>17 more cases across AI generation, SaaS, tourism, CRM, automation, social impact, and internal systems.</p><a class="button solid" href="/en/projects/">Open the full portfolio →</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="voices dark-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="voices-head"><span class="section-label">Client voices</span><h2>Not only<br />my side of the story.</h2></div><div class="quotes"><blockquote><p>“Anton owned our full tech stack, from WeWeb frontend to structuring Xano and building score-calculation APIs. He also helped shape the product vision.”</p><footer>Tobias Weghorn · MetaFox</footer></blockquote><blockquote><p>“He immediately struck me with his clarity and vision of the project. One of the best professionals I have ever met.”</p><footer>Ekaterina Beschastnova · client</footer></blockquote><blockquote><p>“My time spent on client interactions was minimized, and my business grew significantly. Clients regularly praise the convenience of booking.”</p><footer>Dobrosav J. · Dobri Tours</footer></blockquote></div></div></section>
  <section class="identity-note wrap"><div><span class="section-label">Identity note</span><h2>Yes, I have an exact namesake.</h2></div><div><p>Mortimer, associated with “Conscious Mercantilism,” is also named Anton Vladislavovich Nazarov. He is a different person.</p><p>I am <strong>Antiokh</strong>: an IT manager in Belgrade, founder of NeedleBit, and owner of the GitHub profile <strong>Antiokh</strong>.</p><a href="/en/about/">Biography and verified profiles →</a></div></section>
  <section class="contact personal-contact"><div class="wrap"><p class="section-label">If your situation is also “complicated”</p><h2>Tell me the messy version.<br />We’ll work it out.</h2><div><a href="mailto:mail@antiokh.ru">mail@antiokh.ru ↗</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nazarovanton/">LinkedIn ↗</a><a href="https://t.me/antiokh">Telegram ↗</a></div></div></section>
